# Copy to .secrets.env and fill in. Never commit .secrets.env (git-ignored).
# Start with `make oke-bootstrap`: it prints the values this file needs and where to get them.
#
# The tenancy OCID, the region and the compartment are NOT here: they are read from your OCI
# profile (~/.oci/config), which `oci setup config` creates. The compartment defaults to the
# tenancy. The reserved IP and your public CIDR are found by `make oke-tfvars`.

# Optional. No quotes: make passes the value through literally and OKE rejects them.
TF_VAR_ssh_public_key=ssh-ed25519 AAAA... you@laptop

# The public host name served by the ingress. Point its A record at the reserved IP, DNS-only.
HOST=dinner.example.com

# Used by `make oke-up` for the cert-manager ClusterIssuer.
ACME_EMAIL=you@example.com

# Cloudflare API token, scoped to Zone:DNS:Edit and Zone:Zone:Read on the zone that serves HOST.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=REPLACE

# OCIR pull credentials, with the namespace from `make oke-bootstrap`.
# The image path is derived: <region>.ocir.io/<namespace>/dinner-roulette:latest
OCIR_USERNAME=REPLACE
OCIR_AUTH_TOKEN=REPLACE

# Optional. Set only to deploy a tag other than :latest.
# OCIR_IMAGE=eu-milan-1.ocir.io/<namespace>/dinner-roulette:latest

# Optional overrides for tf/variables.tf defaults. Any variable works as TF_VAR_<name>,
# since .secrets.env is exported. The three values `make oke-tfvars` owns (region,
# allowed_source_cidr, lb_reserved_ip_ocid) are written to tf/workshop.auto.tfvars, which
# OpenTofu reads in preference to the environment, so change those with `make oke-tfvars`
# or `make oke-cidr`, not here.
# TF_VAR_node_shape=VM.Standard.E3.Flex
# TF_VAR_node_ocpus=1
# TF_VAR_node_memory_gbs=8
# TF_VAR_k8s_version=v1.34.10
